# The Lamp of the Home

Why does poverty exist in our land where gold is produced? Because Tamil heroes who would challenge it are absent from the legislature. Why did they not enter the legislature? Because the empty talk of idle men prevailed.

Why does deprivation torment a land where iron is found? Because we have no government of our own to awaken the sleeping iron. Why is the government not ours? Because we became enslaved to the North. Why does the North prosper? Through its power to exploit the South. Why does it possess that power? Because the government sits in Delhi.

Why was the government established in Delhi? Because those who spoke of nationalism deceived us. Why did Tamils not learn the truth? Because of the distortions of the daily newspapers. Why has the age of distortion not ended? Because ordinary people have not gained clarity of thought.

Why say all this today? So that deception may at least now be dispelled. Why are people caught by deceivers? Because lime is called butter. When will clarity come? When electoral responsibility is understood.

What must those who understand that responsibility do? Find a way to establish a new government. Who seeks renewal in government? The DMK, which performs noble service. Do you want Congress rule? Would you desire a forest fire? The DMK is the lamp of the home and the true servant of the nation. Light the household lamp and secure the welfare of the country!

---NOTES---
The poem is structured as a chain of political questions and answers. “Lime called butter” is an image of fraudulent substitution, while the home lamp contrasts with the destructive forest fire.

